# Optional. The full https URL this site is served from.
#
# When set, the build emits og:url and canonical tags on every page, a robots.txt sitemap pointer,
# sitemap.xml, and a CNAME file for a GitHub Pages custom domain.
# When unset, all of those are omitted and the site deploys to the default
# *.github.io URL.
#
# A path mounts the site below the origin's root, as a GitHub project page is:
# https://user.github.io/repo. Every link, fetch and image is then written from there, and no
# CNAME is emitted, since a custom domain would serve the site from the root.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. Never commit .env.
#SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com

# Optional. Where each page's file is written, which is up to the host.
#
#   html       (default) `credits.html`, served for `/credits` by a host with clean URLs:
#              GitHub Pages, Neocities, Netlify, Cloudflare. No redirect on a cold load.
#   directory  `credits/index.html`, which any static host serves for `/credits/`. For a host
#              without clean URLs; most redirect `/credits` to `/credits/` and the app tidies
#              the address back up.
#PAGE_LAYOUT=html
